                <pb facs="0730" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg620"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ryan to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 5, 1889</date>.
                        (Received December 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 179.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to this legation’s dispatches
                    Nos. 164 and 166 of the 15th and 16th of November last, I beg to submit further
                    correspondence bearing on the case of Captain Stilphen, of the American schooner
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Robert Ruff</hi>. You will observe that Captain
                    Stilphen is out on bail, and that Mr. Mariscal has requested, through the
                    Treasury Department, a speedy settlement of the matter.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. Ryan.</hi></signed></closer>





